{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhPYNXkhf9HnVjqWpf7N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I built the experiment-1 jsPsych page and its two companion files in `experiment1/experiment/`. I couldn't run the pipeline's own validator because this node has no usable Python environment for the repo. I went through `_validate_implement` line by line and the page should meet every check. Node also parsed the page's JavaScript without errors.\n\n- **`index.html`**: the fixed template, with only the stimuli and the project's wording filled in.\n  - **Order:** an instructions page with a `Begin` button comes first, then 64 trials, then the debrief with a `Finish` button. There is no consent screen, since deployment adds that.\n  - **Wording:** the instructions, the prompt \"Which sequence looks more random?\", the `Left`/`Right` buttons and the debrief are copied word for word from the problem definition. Bold text is rendered as `<strong>`, so participants never see asterisks, and the instructions and debrief sit in the `auto-psych-prose` container.\n  - **Trials:** every trial uses button responses only. Each one randomly decides which sequence goes on the left, and records `sequence_a` as the sequence shown on the left, `sequence_b` as the one on the right, and `chose_left`.\n  - **Stimuli:** all 64 from `design/stimuli.json` are embedded unchanged, and the copy in the page matches the design file exactly.\n  - **Other rules:** there is no fixation cross, no submission code and no root-relative paths. When the experiment finishes, it puts the data in `window.__experimentData`.\n- **`config.json`** is `{ \"experiment_url\": null }`.\n- **`stimuli.json`** is a byte-identical copy of `design/stimuli.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":392,"cache_read_input_tokens":52654,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5